DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270104T210000Z
DTEND:20270104T233000Z
SUMMARY:Shuttle to Ford Island · USS Missouri
DESCRIPTION:The deck where Japan signed the surrender\; grab a simple lunch
  on the island afterwards.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/sea
 rch/?api=1&query=Battleship%20Missouri%20Memorial
LOCATION:Battleship Missouri Memorial
GEO:21.3621708;-157.9533179
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Battleshi
 p Missouri Memorial":geo:21.3621708,-157.9533179
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d2-5@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270104T233000Z
DTEND:20270105T013000Z
SUMMARY:Pearl Harbor Aviation Museum
DESCRIPTION:Two hangars\, ~1.5 hours. Shuttle back to the visitor center af
 terwards.\n\nPassport to Pearl Harbor: https://www.pearlharborhistoricsite
 s.org/tickets\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&quer
 y=Pearl%20Harbor%20Aviation%20Museum
LOCATION:Pearl Harbor Aviation Museum
GEO:21.3588442;-157.9629042
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Pearl Har
 bor Aviation Museum":geo:21.3588442,-157.9629042
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d2-6@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270105T013000Z
DTEND:20270105T023000Z
SUMMARY:Back to Waikīkī
DESCRIPTION:After the aviation museum\, shuttle back to the visitor center\
 , then Uber ~25 min\, arriving around 16:00.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.g
 oogle.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hotel%20Renew%2C%20129%20Paoakalani%20A
 ve%2C%20Honolulu
LOCATION:Hotel Renew\, 129 Paoakalani Ave\, Honolulu
GEO:21.2727845;-157.8222219
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Hotel Ren
 ew, 129 Paoakalani Ave, Honolulu":geo:21.2727845,-157.8222219
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d2-7@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270105T023000Z
DTEND:20270105T050000Z
SUMMARY:Backup: Waikīkī sunset sail
DESCRIPTION:The sunset sail can be today or Jan 7: check the weather and se
 a conditions before the trip and pick whichever day is calmer with fewer c
 louds. If today\, be at the beach boarding spot at 16:30\, sailing 17:00
 –19:00\; you'll still be adjusting to the time change\, so if you're tir
 ed save it for Jan 7. No sail? Stroll Kūhiō Beach and watch the sunset (
 ~18:05 in January).\n\nBook Moana Sailing: https://www.hawaiiactivities.co
 m/en/hawaii/oahu/a/166886\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search
 /?api=1&query=K%C5%ABhi%C5%8D%20Beach%2C%20Honolulu
LOCATION:Kūhiō Beach\, Honolulu
GEO:21.275;-157.82694
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Kūhiō B
 each, Honolulu":geo:21.275,-157.82694
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d2-8@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270105T043000Z
DTEND:20270105T053000Z
SUMMARY:Dinner: Duke's Waikiki
DESCRIPTION:Oceanfront\; fish and Hula Pie. Reserve ahead\; if you sail tod
 ay\, book 19:15.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1
 &query=Duke's%20Waikiki
LOCATION:Duke's Waikiki
GEO:21.2768421;-157.8277917
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Duke's Wa
 ikiki":geo:21.2768421,-157.8277917
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-0@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270105T181500Z
DTEND:20270105T190000Z
SUMMARY:Pick up the car in Waikīkī
DESCRIPTION:Bring your G licence and credit card\; inspect the car and take
  photos. Clockwise loop today: the northeast valleys first\, then back alo
 ng the North Shore.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?ap
 i=1&query=Waik%C4%ABk%C4%AB%20rental%20office%20(sample%20location)
LOCATION:Waikīkī rental office (sample location)
GEO:21.2734513;-157.8222713
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Waikīkī
  rental office (sample location)":geo:21.2734513,-157.8222713
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-1@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270105T190000Z
DTEND:20270105T200500Z
SUMMARY:Hoʻomaluhia Botanical Garden
DESCRIPTION:Opens at 9:00. Drive in\, park by the lake for mountain photos\
 , and walk a short stretch. Skipping Byodo-In this time\, so you can linge
 r here.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ho
 %CA%BBomaluhia%20Botanical%20Garden
LOCATION:Hoʻomaluhia Botanical Garden
GEO:21.3882747;-157.8070148
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Hoʻomalu
 hia Botanical Garden":geo:21.3882747,-157.8070148
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-2@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270105T210000Z
DTEND:20270105T233000Z
SUMMARY:Kualoa Ranch Jurassic Adventure
DESCRIPTION:Check in at the ranch around 10:40. Ride an off-road vehicle in
 to the Kualoa\, Hakipuʻu and Kaʻaʻawa valleys to see filming spots from
  Jurassic Park\, Jurassic World and more. Bumpy ride\, only short walks. B
 ook your slot ahead.\n\nKualoa official site: https://www.kualoa.com/tours
 /\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kualoa%20R
 anch
LOCATION:Kualoa Ranch
GEO:21.5208318;-157.8372577
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Kualoa Ra
 nch":geo:21.5208318,-157.8372577
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-3@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T000500Z
DTEND:20270106T004000Z
SUMMARY:Giovanni's garlic shrimp
DESCRIPTION:Lunch. If the line is too long\, try Romy's or Fumi's next door
 . Then head west on Kamehameha Hwy\; just glance at Shark's Cove and Waime
 a Bay from the car: North Shore surf is big on winter afternoons\, so no d
 edicated stops.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&
 query=Giovanni's%20Shrimp%20Truck%2C%20Kahuku
LOCATION:Giovanni's Shrimp Truck\, Kahuku
GEO:21.677198;-157.9484211
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Giovanni'
 s Shrimp Truck, Kahuku":geo:21.677198,-157.9484211
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-4@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T010500Z
DTEND:20270106T012000Z
SUMMARY:Turtle watching at Laniakea
DESCRIPTION:Turtles often haul out to bask in the afternoon\; watch from sh
 ore for 15 min and keep your distance. Roadside parking is tight\; if ther
 e's no spot\, go straight to Dole.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/
 maps/search/?api=1&query=Laniakea%20Beach
LOCATION:Laniakea Beach
GEO:21.6187;-158.0853
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Laniakea 
 Beach":geo:21.6187,-158.0853
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-5@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T014000Z
DTEND:20270106T033000Z
SUMMARY:Dole Plantation: train + maze
DESCRIPTION:Ride the Pineapple Express train first (~20 min\, roughly every
  10 min\; the official site suggests 1 hour including the pineapple-cuttin
 g demo)\, then the Pineapple Garden Maze (40 min on average)\, and finish 
 with Dole Whip. Park hours 9:30–17:30\; the last train and last maze ent
 ry aren't listed online\, so call 808-621-8408 before you go. If the last 
 train is early\, do the maze first.\n\nDole Plantation official site: http
 s://www.doleplantation.com/\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/sear
 ch/?api=1&query=Dole%20Plantation
LOCATION:Dole Plantation
GEO:21.5259081;-158.0378039
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Dole Plan
 tation":geo:21.5259081,-158.0378039
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-6@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T035000Z
DTEND:20270106T044000Z
SUMMARY:Waikele Premium Outlets
DESCRIPTION:~20 min from Dole via H-2. Shop for ~50 min only\; if you run l
 ate at Dole\, skip it and go straight to Ko Olina for dinner.\n\nOutlets o
 fficial site: https://www.premiumoutlets.com/outlet/waikele\nGoogle Maps: 
 https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Waikele%20Premium%20Outlet
 s
LOCATION:Waikele Premium Outlets
GEO:21.4017617;-158.0068567
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Waikele P
 remium Outlets":geo:21.4017617,-158.0068567
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-7@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T050000Z
DTEND:20270106T055000Z
SUMMARY:Ko Olina dinner
DESCRIPTION:~18 min drive from the outlets (~35 min straight from Dole). Ea
 t inside the Ko Olina resort area\, e.g. Monkeypod Kitchen\; reservations 
 recommended.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&que
 ry=Four%20Seasons%20Resort%20Oahu%20at%20Ko%20Olina
LOCATION:Four Seasons Resort Oahu at Ko Olina
GEO:21.3392955;-158.125741
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Four Seas
 ons Resort Oahu at Ko Olina":geo:21.3392955,-158.125741
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-8@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T060000Z
DTEND:20270106T070000Z
SUMMARY:Stargazing · Stars Above Hawaii
DESCRIPTION:An astronomy guide with a computerized telescope talks about Ha
 waiian star navigation\, ~1 hour\, and photos are sent to your phone. Jan 
 7 is the new moon\, so these are the darkest nights. Start time depends on
  the slot you book\; you'll get a text that afternoon about weather and th
 e viewing spot. Weather cancellations get a full refund or rebooking.\n\nB
 ooking page: https://www.greetwell.com/us/direct/stargazing-star-show-ko-o
 lina-resort\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=
 Four%20Seasons%20Resort%20Oahu%20at%20Ko%20Olina
LOCATION:Four Seasons Resort Oahu at Ko Olina
GEO:21.3392955;-158.125741
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Four Seas
 ons Resort Oahu at Ko Olina":geo:21.3392955,-158.125741
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d3-9@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T070000Z
DTEND:20270106T080000Z
SUMMARY:Drive back to Waikīkī
DESCRIPTION:~45 min\, back at the hotel around 21:45. Take it easy on the r
 oads at night\; it's a long day. Park at the hotel overnight (~USD45) and 
 return the car tomorrow morning.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/ma
 ps/search/?api=1&query=Hotel%20Renew%2C%20129%20Paoakalani%20Ave%2C%20Hono
 lulu
LOCATION:Hotel Renew\, 129 Paoakalani Ave\, Honolulu
GEO:21.2727845;-157.8222219
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Hotel Ren
 ew, 129 Paoakalani Ave, Honolulu":geo:21.2727845,-157.8222219
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d4-0@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T180000Z
DTEND:20270106T190000Z
SUMMARY:Fill up and return the car
DESCRIPTION:Return by the time on your booking\; being late may cost an ext
 ra day.\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Wa
 ik%C4%ABk%C4%AB%20rental%20office%20(sample%20location)
LOCATION:Waikīkī rental office (sample location)
GEO:21.2734513;-157.8222713
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Waikīkī
  rental office (sample location)":geo:21.2734513,-157.8222713
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d4-1@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T190000Z
DTEND:20270106T200000Z
SUMMARY:Start the Waikiki Trolley 4-day pass
DESCRIPTION:4-day all-line pass ~USD150 for two\, hop on/hop off\, good for
  Jan 6–8. Take the Red Line (downtown history line) to the palace.\n\nWa
 ikiki Trolley official site: https://waikikitrolley.com/\nGoogle Maps: htt
 ps://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=T%20Galleria%20by%20DFS%2C%20
 Waikiki
LOCATION:T Galleria by DFS\, Waikiki
GEO:21.28;-157.8296
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="T Galleri
 a by DFS, Waikiki":geo:21.28,-157.8296
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d4-2@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T200000Z
DTEND:20270106T213000Z
SUMMARY:ʻIolani Palace
DESCRIPTION:The only royal palace in the US\; open Tue–Sat\, tickets onli
 ne only.\n\nʻIolani Palace official site: https://www.iolanipalace.org/vi
 sit/\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%CA%BBI
 olani%20Palace
LOCATION:ʻIolani Palace
GEO:21.3068147;-157.8587655
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="ʻIolani 
 Palace":geo:21.3068147,-157.8587655
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d4-3@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T213000Z
DTEND:20270106T223000Z
SUMMARY:King Kamehameha Statue\, Chinatown
DESCRIPTION:The statue is right across from the palace\; take the Red Line 
 or walk to Chinatown.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oahu-2027-jan-five-nights-d4-4@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T193122Z
DTSTART:20270106T223000Z
DTEND:20270107T003000Z
SUMMARY:Seafood lunch at Nico's Pier 38
DESCRIPTION:Not on a trolley line\; Uber ~10 min. Poke bowls and fried fish
 .\n\nGoogle Maps: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nico's%2
 0Pier%2038
LOCATION:Nico's Pier 38
GEO:21.3175754;-157.8775063
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Nico's Pi
 er 38":geo:21.3175754,-157.8775063
